{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Let now be taken.</b> Through an agent — and the Holy One, blessed be He, paid back his children through an agent, as it says: ״וַיָּרֶם מֹשֶׁה אֶת יָדוֹ וַיַּךְ אֶת הַסֶּלַע״ (Numbers 20)." "<b>And wash your feet.</b> For he thought they were Arabs who worship the dust of their feet, and he was insistent not to bring idolatry into his house. But Lot, who was not insistent, put lodging before washing, as it says: ״וְלִינוּ וְרַחֲצוּ רַגְלֵיכֶם״." "<b>Under the tree.</b> תַּחַת הָאִילָן."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:08.950212556Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}